(4389550, 629431, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice smile, but too much shine from the lights is unflattering.</td>', 'Nice smile, but too much shine from the lights is unflattering.', '2008-01-13 18:21:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4389552, 630750, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice out of the box thinking here. Did you intentionally set this up, or did it just happen?</td>', 'Nice out of the box thinking here. Did you intentionally set this up, or did it just happen?', '2008-01-13 18:22:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4389555, 629991, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice twist on the theme. It works well.</td>', 'Nice twist on the theme. It works well.', '2008-01-13 18:23:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(4389558, 630584, 83313, '<td valign="top">Excellent. Good comp and use of b/w. the image flows nicely.</td>', 'Excellent. Good comp and use of b/w. the image flows nicely.', '2008-01-13 18:24:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(4389599, 630811, 83313, '<td valign="top">This picture has an awful lot of potential. The pose and expressions are great. As it is, however, it is washed out and pixelated. <br/> <br/>Looking at your file size, you only used about 1/3 the file size that was available to you, and it is showing in a lot of grainy compression artifacts that are clearly visible around high contrast edges, such as around the boys eyes and all along his forearm. If you use less compression when you save the file, you can eliminate most of the visible artifacts. Alway use the lowest compression ration that will get your shot in under the filesize limit for a challenge.<br/> <br/>The washed out color (If it was not an intentional effect) can be largely corrected with adjustments such as levels and curves.</td>', 'This picture has an awful lot of potential. The pose and expressions are great. As it is, however, it is washed out and pixelated.  Looking at your file size, you only used about 1/3 the file size that was available to you, and it is showing in a lot of grainy compression artifacts that are clearly visible around high contrast edges, such as around the boys eyes and all along his forearm. If you use less compression when you save the file, you can eliminate most of the visible artifacts. Alway use the lowest compression ration that will get your shot in under the filesize limit for a challenge. The washed out color (If it was not an intentional effect) can be largely corrected with adjustments such as levels and curves.', '2008-01-13 18:43:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4389601, 629552, 83313, '<td valign="top">He''s glaring at me until I give this picture a high vote.</td>', 'He''s glaring at me until I give this picture a high vote.', '2008-01-13 18:45:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(4389606, 630613, 83313, '<td valign="top">I really like this. Lots of great character coming through. I like the slightly scruffy hair. looks like this was outside with some wind, perhaps.</td>', 'I really like this. Lots of great character coming through. I like the slightly scruffy hair. looks like this was outside with some wind, perhaps.', '2008-01-13 18:47:24.000000', NULL, 1),
