(4397486, 630076, 68035, '<td valign="top">I recognised your boy straight away...and as you said way better without the mohawk.<br/> <br/>I thought this was a lovely shot, especially liked the tilt of the head which contrasted against the zip of his top (great colours by the way).  Super sharp too.  Being a glasses wearer it was the fogging of the lens by the nose that made me laugh though...man we have all been there<br/> <br/></td>', 'I recognised your boy straight away...and as you said way better without the mohawk. I thought this was a lovely shot, especially liked the tilt of the head which contrasted against the zip of his top (great colours by the way).  Super sharp too.  Being a glasses wearer it was the fogging of the lens by the nose that made me laugh though...man we have all been there ', '2008-01-16 15:33:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4397497, 628923, 68035, '<td valign="top">Peter, I meant to comment on this shot during the challenge but with the new job I am afraid my DPC time has been somewhat restricted.  I thought this was a super portrait (and of course I did recognise you straight away).  Great expression too.<br/> <br/>Your doing a great job with your new lighting rig as well love the way your face is framed to the left and right by blackness, very effective, especially as your hair and sweater provide top/bottom framing as well<br/> <br/>As ever sharpness, colour and dof are spot on.  Super shot</td>', 'Peter, I meant to comment on this shot during the challenge but with the new job I am afraid my DPC time has been somewhat restricted.  I thought this was a super portrait (and of course I did recognise you straight away).  Great expression too. Your doing a great job with your new lighting rig as well love the way your face is framed to the left and right by blackness, very effective, especially as your hair and sweater provide top/bottom framing as well As ever sharpness, colour and dof are spot on.  Super shot', '2008-01-16 15:38:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4397511, 630704, 68035, '<td valign="top">Lovely diagonal corner framing in this shot and a fantastic job of catching the loyalty and devotion of the dog towards its owner (which is clearly reciprocated) in just one eye<br/> <br/>Great sharpness and the bokeh works well.  I dont know if you have the expression in the States but in England we say that people begin to look like their pets and given this the comparison between the beard and the grey hairs on the muzzle made me smile<br/> <br/>As Michelle mentioned I like the fact that this was a picture in its own right that included someone wearing glasses rather than a picture of glasses which someone happened to be wearing</td>', 'Lovely diagonal corner framing in this shot and a fantastic job of catching the loyalty and devotion of the dog towards its owner (which is clearly reciprocated) in just one eye Great sharpness and the bokeh works well.  I dont know if you have the expression in the States but in England we say that people begin to look like their pets and given this the comparison between the beard and the grey hairs on the muzzle made me smile As Michelle mentioned I like the fact that this was a picture in its own right that included someone wearing glasses rather than a picture of glasses which someone happened to be wearing', '2008-01-16 15:44:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4397536, 630342, 68035, '<td valign="top">Lisa, your family is doubly blessed, firstly in having a daughter as beautiful as this and secondly in her having a mother who can capture this beauty so wonderfully<br/> <br/>Another lovely portrait, super composition, dof and sharpness and I love the complimentary colours of glasses and her top.<br/> <br/>I am glad that she is so good with her glasses as a fellow spectacle wearer i can empathise with the fact that they can be a nuisance but remind her that it is only great works of art that get framed not the everyday</td>', 'Lisa, your family is doubly blessed, firstly in having a daughter as beautiful as this and secondly in her having a mother who can capture this beauty so wonderfully Another lovely portrait, super composition, dof and sharpness and I love the complimentary colours of glasses and her top. I am glad that she is so good with her glasses as a fellow spectacle wearer i can empathise with the fact that they can be a nuisance but remind her that it is only great works of art that get framed not the everyday', '2008-01-16 15:55:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4397560, 630781, 86799, '<td valign="top">I''m disappointed for you on this score.  I still like it, even if only from the challenge it presents.  I''ve read that same book, several times...but I still can''t remember where it ever said you have to read it with clothes on, or that God is offended by the body He created.  Hmmm.</td>', 'I''m disappointed for you on this score.  I still like it, even if only from the challenge it presents.  I''ve read that same book, several times...but I still can''t remember where it ever said you have to read it with clothes on, or that God is offended by the body He created.  Hmmm.', '2008-01-16 16:05:41.000000', NULL, 0),
