(4399871, 630781, 85886, '<td valign="top">Wow!  I''m blown away this didn''t at least reach a 6.  The sheer volume of 1-4s pretty much indicates how strongly the DPC voters feel about the religious implications.  Staggering.  It''s a woman reading the bible in just about a shirt - what''s so blasphemous or distasteful about that?  There is nothing sexual about the piece, explicitly or implicitly.  She is merely reading a bible.  Had the shot not shown 5mm of almost nipple then I doubt anyone would have blinked an eyelid, but ooooh there''s just the tiniest bit of nipple.  The naked body is not always some kind of pornographic or sexual device and calling it out in this manner is crying wolf on my planet.  I''m sorry but to find this offensive on a photography site is really closed minded and in my opinion completely contrary to the photographic and creative process....and is really disappointing.</td>', 'Wow!  I''m blown away this didn''t at least reach a 6.  The sheer volume of 1-4s pretty much indicates how strongly the DPC voters feel about the religious implications.  Staggering.  It''s a woman reading the bible in just about a shirt - what''s so blasphemous or distasteful about that?  There is nothing sexual about the piece, explicitly or implicitly.  She is merely reading a bible.  Had the shot not shown 5mm of almost nipple then I doubt anyone would have blinked an eyelid, but ooooh there''s just the tiniest bit of nipple.  The naked body is not always some kind of pornographic or sexual device and calling it out in this manner is crying wolf on my planet.  I''m sorry but to find this offensive on a photography site is really closed minded and in my opinion completely contrary to the photographic and creative process....and is really disappointing.', '2008-01-17 12:18:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4400240, 630781, 5885, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Quasimojo:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m sorry but to find this offensive on a photography site is really closed minded and in my opinion completely contrary to the photographic and creative process....and is really disappointing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nick, I appreciate your views and statements. I''ve found, however, that people in general are close-minded. It''s not just religious zealots or "fanatics". All people are close-minded to some extent. Why else do I, myself, continue to force nudes on a crowd that obviously dislikes them? Is it because I am somehow more enlightened? No, it''s not. It''s because I''m stubborn. <br/> <br/>Seriously, I know I could produce "DPCish" images and do well here, but I want to stand out and be known for MY style of photography, whatever that may be. I''m stubborn enough that I''ll continue to take the lower scores, until <br/>A) DPCers change (not likely) <br/>B) I change (also not likely) or <br/>C) I get lucky.<br/>That in itself makes ME close-minded and fanatical about pushing racy images. But, so be it. I''m human, just like those that would be called zealots. We each have our views and neither is likely to change.</td>', 'Originally posted by Quasimojo: I''m sorry but to find this offensive on a photography site is really closed minded and in my opinion completely contrary to the photographic and creative process....and is really disappointing.   Nick, I appreciate your views and statements. I''ve found, however, that people in general are close-minded. It''s not just religious zealots or "fanatics". All people are close-minded to some extent. Why else do I, myself, continue to force nudes on a crowd that obviously dislikes them? Is it because I am somehow more enlightened? No, it''s not. It''s because I''m stubborn.  Seriously, I know I could produce "DPCish" images and do well here, but I want to stand out and be known for MY style of photography, whatever that may be. I''m stubborn enough that I''ll continue to take the lower scores, until A) DPCers change (not likely) B) I change (also not likely) or C) I get lucky.That in itself makes ME close-minded and fanatical about pushing racy images. But, so be it. I''m human, just like those that would be called zealots. We each have our views and neither is likely to change.', '2008-01-17 14:25:16.000000', NULL, 0),
