(4406628, 628845, 55838, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by timfythetoo:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by digifotojo:</b></div><hr/><i> Not sure why this took first place, it''s burned out and not very interesting. Hmm </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I think it took first place because it had the highest overall average. But I could be mistaken. ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I think it was those great glasses...yeah...it was the cool glasses!  Beautiful shot of our wee babe!  Adding to fav''s of course!</td>', 'Originally posted by timfythetoo: Originally posted by digifotojo: Not sure why this took first place, it''s burned out and not very interesting. Hmm  I think it took first place because it had the highest overall average. But I could be mistaken. ;)  I think it was those great glasses...yeah...it was the cool glasses!  Beautiful shot of our wee babe!  Adding to fav''s of course!', '2008-01-20 14:05:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4406629, 630770, 57229, '<td valign="top">I wonder if I should feel guilty that I didn''t give this my OOBIE vote, as it is probably the most out of box (out of mind?) entry. My heart lay elsewhere. This is a great idea and brilliantly done - heh. I can all but smell it...</td>', 'I wonder if I should feel guilty that I didn''t give this my OOBIE vote, as it is probably the most out of box (out of mind?) entry. My heart lay elsewhere. This is a great idea and brilliantly done - heh. I can all but smell it...', '2008-01-20 14:06:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4406632, 629415, 57229, '<td valign="top">I''d go as far as to say that it''s silly, but a great idea and very well done. Thanks for adding spice to the bespectacled portrait experience.</td>', 'I''d go as far as to say that it''s silly, but a great idea and very well done. Thanks for adding spice to the bespectacled portrait experience.', '2008-01-20 14:08:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4408347, 628845, 67841, '<td valign="top">Wow, it''s not often my top pick actually makes it.  Congrats!!!</td>', 'Wow, it''s not often my top pick actually makes it.  Congrats!!!', '2008-01-21 00:31:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4409945, 628845, 70828, '<td valign="top">I think everything ... the mood the lighting the DOF the expression ... but sheesh ... that really really really hard sharpened edge under the top lip makes me cringe. It seems such a small fault with an absolutely gorgeous portrait.<br/> <br/>Please don''t get me wrong ... it is actually INCREDIBLE in all other ways ... It just looks like the bottom of her top lip was cut with scissors IMO.<br/> <br/>... sorry ... but I thought you would like everyone''s opinion ... please send me an email to tell me if you agree or disagree so I don''t feel so guilty?<br/> <br/>Edited later ... <br/> <br/>oh ... STUPID me. I did not even think about looking at the editing rules allowed for the shot and did not notice it was Basic Editing Rules. I can see how this happened now and LOVE the shot and now realize that that lip halo would not be there on a full size image. It IS a beautiful image and something else that I just realized ... a PERFECT example of how rules should be broken in some instances and better for her looking OUT of the shot rather than in.  <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-21 20:39:28.</i></td>', 'I think everything ... the mood the lighting the DOF the expression ... but sheesh ... that really really really hard sharpened edge under the top lip makes me cringe. It seems such a small fault with an absolutely gorgeous portrait. Please don''t get me wrong ... it is actually INCREDIBLE in all other ways ... It just looks like the bottom of her top lip was cut with scissors IMO. ... sorry ... but I thought you would like everyone''s opinion ... please send me an email to tell me if you agree or disagree so I don''t feel so guilty? Edited later ...  oh ... STUPID me. I did not even think about looking at the editing rules allowed for the shot and did not notice it was Basic Editing Rules. I can see how this happened now and LOVE the shot and now realize that that lip halo would not be there on a full size image. It IS a beautiful image and something else that I just realized ... a PERFECT example of how rules should be broken in some instances and better for her looking OUT of the shot rather than in.  ', '2008-01-21 11:05:34.000000', '2008-01-21 20:39:28.000000', 0),
(4410649, 630637, 51386, '<td valign="top">I am not surprised that this is one of yours. As always, I love the creative image. Excellent idea.</td>', 'I am not surprised that this is one of yours. As always, I love the creative image. Excellent idea.', '2008-01-21 13:49:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4412557, 630756, 88575, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ArpeggioAngel:</b></div><hr/><i> Would love to know how you got this guy to stay still not just with glasses but with a hat too! Kudos to you just for that effort alone!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It wasn''t hard to do.  He is so sweet and gentle.  He actually wore the glasses around for about 30 minutes until I took them off.</td>', 'Originally posted by ArpeggioAngel: Would love to know how you got this guy to stay still not just with glasses but with a hat too! Kudos to you just for that effort alone!!   It wasn''t hard to do.  He is so sweet and gentle.  He actually wore the glasses around for about 30 minutes until I took them off.', '2008-01-21 23:56:59.000000', NULL, 0),
