(4420266, 630544, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent!  Did you use native mud?  :-)  Really a nice portrait.  I''m not at all understanding the 1s and 2s.  Not at all.</td>', 'Excellent!  Did you use native mud?  :-)  Really a nice portrait.  I''m not at all understanding the 1s and 2s.  Not at all.', '2008-01-24 04:25:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4420386, 630432, 64032, '<td valign="top">Great picture and thanks for explaining in detail how you made it. You gave me an interesting idea about lighting.</td>', 'Great picture and thanks for explaining in detail how you made it. You gave me an interesting idea about lighting.', '2008-01-24 06:13:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4423263, 630626, 69008, '<td valign="top">As the others said, there is too much apple in this image.  I understand that in order to capture the moment, you had to compose and shoot quickly.  It''s a tough bunch of voters here at DPC, so don''t be discouraged by not placing higher in the scoring.  I have a 4.5 and a DQ in my challenge shots.  You are seeing the "moment" in your shots already, and with some time to learn, about composition and camera settings, I feel that you will soon be improving your scores a lot as you gain experience.</td>', 'As the others said, there is too much apple in this image.  I understand that in order to capture the moment, you had to compose and shoot quickly.  It''s a tough bunch of voters here at DPC, so don''t be discouraged by not placing higher in the scoring.  I have a 4.5 and a DQ in my challenge shots.  You are seeing the "moment" in your shots already, and with some time to learn, about composition and camera settings, I feel that you will soon be improving your scores a lot as you gain experience.', '2008-01-24 23:17:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4423569, 629415, 53316, '<td valign="top">Wow, a really neat take on the challenge, especially with the title.</td>', 'Wow, a really neat take on the challenge, especially with the title.', '2008-01-25 02:18:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4423574, 630770, 53316, '<td valign="top">OH MY GOODNESS this is so awesome.  LOL LOL.  And I really do think it fits the challenge, too, although at the same time being out of the box.  Which is what I really like - the combination of those two.<br/> <br/>And the title is awesome, as the long "nose" is good for smelling but it''s also a pet''s butt and that''s just so funny.<br/> <br/>Annnd.... the picture is just a good-quality one!  I love the tones and I think the depth of field really accentuates the "face" part of things and the composition is good.<br/> <br/>Yay!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-25 02:21:32.</i></td>', 'OH MY GOODNESS this is so awesome.  LOL LOL.  And I really do think it fits the challenge, too, although at the same time being out of the box.  Which is what I really like - the combination of those two. And the title is awesome, as the long "nose" is good for smelling but it''s also a pet''s butt and that''s just so funny. Annnd.... the picture is just a good-quality one!  I love the tones and I think the depth of field really accentuates the "face" part of things and the composition is good. Yay!', '2008-01-25 02:19:50.000000', '2008-01-25 02:21:32.000000', 0),
(4424077, 629882, 61961, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.  I prefer the composition on this one as compared to your outtake, though the outtake seems a bit sharper.  Love the sense of movement in both.</td>', 'Beautiful.  I prefer the composition on this one as compared to your outtake, though the outtake seems a bit sharper.  Love the sense of movement in both.', '2008-01-25 11:15:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4425626, 630781, 66635, '<td valign="top">Holy Toledo!</td>', 'Holy Toledo!', '2008-01-25 23:26:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426411, 630517, 48471, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised by the high number of confused commenters that didn''t see the self portait immediately. I think it''s quite emphasised, more than the portrait of the girl...<br/>I like the play and double interpretations that this image offers: there''s a picture framed by her sunglasses, a very good picture in its own right, and the title asks the viewer to pay attention to it. But, then, there is this portrait of this lady, and one might think that the being of the photographer has a meaning only because of her. So, she should be the subject, she should be the topic of this photo. But no, wait a sec, what''s she thinking about, why does she take this pose? And the answer: because there''s a photographer there, again he gets all the attention. To state the obvious: the photographer doesn''t ruin the photo, he is the photo. Narcissist, I''d say.</td>', 'I''m surprised by the high number of confused commenters that didn''t see the self portait immediately. I think it''s quite emphasised, more than the portrait of the girl...I like the play and double interpretations that this image offers: there''s a picture framed by her sunglasses, a very good picture in its own right, and the title asks the viewer to pay attention to it. But, then, there is this portrait of this lady, and one might think that the being of the photographer has a meaning only because of her. So, she should be the subject, she should be the topic of this photo. But no, wait a sec, what''s she thinking about, why does she take this pose? And the answer: because there''s a photographer there, again he gets all the attention. To state the obvious: the photographer doesn''t ruin the photo, he is the photo. Narcissist, I''d say.', '2008-01-26 12:40:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4427350, 629882, 714, '<td valign="top">This is a gorgeous shot but one thing that bugs me is her nose looks flat.  Maybe shade her nose a little bit more to give it depth.</td>', 'This is a gorgeous shot but one thing that bugs me is her nose looks flat.  Maybe shade her nose a little bit more to give it depth.', '2008-01-26 20:48:51.000000', NULL, 0),
